IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-22: Article 22 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): authorised representatives of providers of high-risk AI systems.
-- Lines 435-446 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus. Article 2(13) names Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25, so Article 22 is among those whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system (the gate).
-- Parties: the provider (paragraphs 1 and 2) and the authorised representative (paragraphs 3 and 4). The role of authorised representative is Art 3(5); the keel decides it.
-- Seam: Article 22(1) is cited by Article 23(1)(d) (the importer verifies the appointment).
-- "Prior to making their high-risk AI systems available on the Union market": the deadline of the appointment rule is the placement date in the `AI system` record (the first making available), inclusive; fork F-prior-to.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met; JUST FALSE the duty applies and is not met; NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, Art 2(13) may limit the Article, or the paragraph limits itself).

DECLARE `Art 22 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 22(1) appoint, by written mandate, an authorised representative which is established in the Union`
    `Art 22(2) enable the authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate`
    `Art 22(3) perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider`
    `Art 22(3) provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities`
    `Art 22(4) terminate the mandate`
    `Art 22(4) inform the relevant market surveillance authority and, where applicable, the relevant notified body about the termination and the reasons`

§ `Article 22(1): a provider established in a third country appoints an authorised representative by written mandate before making its system available`

-- src:437 | 1. Prior to making their high-risk AI systems available on the Union market, providers established in third countries shall, by written mandate, appoint an authorised representative which is established in the Union.
@ref Art 22(1) (src:437)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider's place` IS A `Place of a party`
      `the provider has appointed an authorised representative by written mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative is established in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(1) the provider established in a third country has appointed an authorised representative by written mandate` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the provider's place` EQUALS `Established or located in a third country`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "providers established in third countries shall, by written mandate, appoint an authorised representative" (the provider is not established in a third country)
        ELSE
             IF `the provider has appointed an authorised representative by written mandate` AND `the authorised representative is established in the Union`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Prior to making their high-risk AI systems available on the Union market, providers established in third countries shall, by written mandate, appoint an authorised representative which is established in the Union"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)

@ref Art 22(1) (src:437)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider's place` IS A `Place of a party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 22 act`
`Art 22(1) the provider's duty to appoint an authorised representative by written mandate prior to making its high-risk AI system available on the Union market` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the provider's place` EQUALS `Established or located in a third country`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 22(1) appoint, by written mandate, an authorised representative which is established in the Union`
         WITHIN daysLeft
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "no authorised representative was appointed by written mandate before the high-risk AI system was made available on the Union market"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the provider is not established in a third country
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)
        placed MEANS `the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`
        daysLeft MEANS IF (Day placed) AT LEAST (Day `the date asked`) THEN (Day placed) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) ELSE 0


§ `Article 22(2): the provider enables its authorised representative`

-- src:438 | 2. The provider shall enable its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider.
@ref Art 22(2) (src:438)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider has enabled its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(2) the provider has enabled its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the provider has enabled its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provider shall enable its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)

@ref Art 22(2) (src:438)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 22 act`
`Art 22(2) the provider's duty to enable its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 22(2) enable the authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the authorised representative was not enabled to perform the tasks specified in the mandate"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)


§ `Article 22(3): the authorised representative performs the tasks of the mandate and provides a copy of it upon request`

-- src:439 | 3. The authorised representative shall perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider. It shall provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request, in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority. For the purposes of this Regulation, the mandate shall empower the authorised representative to carry out the following tasks:
@ref Art 22(3) first sentence (src:439)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the authorised representative performs the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(3) the authorised representative performs the tasks specified in the mandate` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the authorised representative performs the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authorised representative shall perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)

@ref Art 22(3) first sentence (src:439)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 22 act`
`Art 22(3) the authorised representative's duty to perform the tasks specified in the mandate` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY `Authorised representative`
         MUST `Art 22(3) perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Authorised representative` BECAUSE "the tasks specified in the mandate were not performed"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)


-- src:439 | 3. The authorised representative shall perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider. It shall provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request, in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority. For the purposes of this Regulation, the mandate shall empower the authorised representative to carry out the following tasks:
@ref Art 22(3) second sentence (src:439)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the copy is in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(3) the authorised representative has provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It shall provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request" (no request has been made)
        ELSE
             IF `the authorised representative has provided a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities` AND `the copy is in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It shall provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request, in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)

@ref Art 22(3) second sentence (src:439)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 22 act`
`Art 22(3) the authorised representative's duty to provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `a market surveillance authority has requested a copy of the mandate`
    THEN PARTY `Authorised representative`
         MUST `Art 22(3) provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Authorised representative` BECAUSE "a copy of the mandate was not provided to the market surveillance authorities"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or no request has been made
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)


§ `Article 22(3)(a) to (e) and the last sentence: what the mandate shall empower the authorised representative to do`

-- The text does not name who must draft the mandate that way: it says what the mandate "shall empower". The decision function therefore asks about the mandate (a plain record of seven facts);
-- there is no regulative rule for it (coverage row: encoded, no party named).
-- src:440 | (a) verify that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and the technical documentation referred to in Article 11 have been drawn up and that an appropriate conformity assessment procedure has been carried out by the provider;
-- src:441 | (b) keep at the disposal of the competent authorities and national authorities or bodies referred to in Article 74(10), for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, the contact details of the provider that appointed the authorised representative, a copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47, the technical documentation and, if applicable, the certificate issued by the notified body;
-- src:442 | (c) provide a competent authority, upon a reasoned request, with all the information and documentation, including that referred to in point (b) of this subparagraph, necessary to demonstrate the conformity of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2, including access to the logs, as referred to in Article 12(1), automatically generated by the high-risk AI system, to the extent such logs are under the control of the provider;
-- src:443 | (d) cooperate with competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, in any action the latter take in relation to the high-risk AI system, in particular to reduce and mitigate the risks posed by the high-risk AI system;
-- src:444 | (e) where applicable, comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1), or, if the registration is carried out by the provider itself, ensure that the information referred to in point 3 of Section A of Annex VIII is correct.
@ref Art 22(3)(a) to (e) (src:440-444)
DECLARE `Art 22(3) what the mandate empowers the authorised representative to do` HAS
    `verify the declaration of conformity, the technical documentation and the conformity assessment procedure`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a) verify that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and the technical documentation referred to in Article 11 have been drawn up and that an appropriate conformity assessment procedure has been carried out by the provider
    `keep at the disposal of the authorities for 10 years the provider's contact details, the declaration, the technical documentation and the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b) for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service
    `provide a competent authority upon a reasoned request with all the information and documentation, including access to the logs` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `cooperate with competent authorities in any action in relation to the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d) upon a reasoned request, in particular to reduce and mitigate the risks
    `there are registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (e) "where applicable"
    `comply with the registration obligations or, if the provider registers, ensure the information is correct` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (e)
    `be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities on all issues related to ensuring compliance` IS A BOOLEAN  -- the last sentence

-- src:439 | 3. The authorised representative shall perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider. It shall provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request, in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority. For the purposes of this Regulation, the mandate shall empower the authorised representative to carry out the following tasks:
-- src:440 | (a) verify that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and the technical documentation referred to in Article 11 have been drawn up and that an appropriate conformity assessment procedure has been carried out by the provider;
-- src:441 | (b) keep at the disposal of the competent authorities and national authorities or bodies referred to in Article 74(10), for a period of 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, the contact details of the provider that appointed the authorised representative, a copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47, the technical documentation and, if applicable, the certificate issued by the notified body;
-- src:442 | (c) provide a competent authority, upon a reasoned request, with all the information and documentation, including that referred to in point (b) of this subparagraph, necessary to demonstrate the conformity of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2, including access to the logs, as referred to in Article 12(1), automatically generated by the high-risk AI system, to the extent such logs are under the control of the provider;
-- src:443 | (d) cooperate with competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, in any action the latter take in relation to the high-risk AI system, in particular to reduce and mitigate the risks posed by the high-risk AI system;
-- src:444 | (e) where applicable, comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1), or, if the registration is carried out by the provider itself, ensure that the information referred to in point 3 of Section A of Annex VIII is correct.
-- src:445 | The mandate shall empower the authorised representative to be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities, on all issues related to ensuring compliance with this Regulation.
@ref Art 22(3) mandate (src:439-445)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the mandate` IS AN `Art 22(3) what the mandate empowers the authorised representative to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(3) the mandate empowers the authorised representative to carry out the tasks` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF       `the mandate`'s `verify the declaration of conformity, the technical documentation and the conformity assessment procedure`
             AND `the mandate`'s `keep at the disposal of the authorities for 10 years the provider's contact details, the declaration, the technical documentation and the certificate`
             AND `the mandate`'s `provide a competent authority upon a reasoned request with all the information and documentation, including access to the logs`
             AND `the mandate`'s `cooperate with competent authorities in any action in relation to the high-risk AI system`
             AND ((NOT `the mandate`'s `there are registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)`) OR `the mandate`'s `comply with the registration obligations or, if the provider registers, ensure the information is correct`)
             AND `the mandate`'s `be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities on all issues related to ensuring compliance`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the mandate shall empower the authorised representative to carry out the following tasks: (a) ... (e)" and "The mandate shall empower the authorised representative to be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)

§ `Article 22(4): the authorised representative terminates the mandate and then informs "immediately"`

-- src:446 | 4. The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation. In such a case, it shall immediately inform the relevant market surveillance authority, as well as, where applicable, the relevant notified body, about the termination of the mandate and the reasons therefor.
@ref Art 22(4) first sentence (src:446)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the authorised representative considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has terminated the mandate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(4) the authorised representative has terminated the mandate` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the authorised representative considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations" (it has no such reason)
        ELSE
             IF `the authorised representative has terminated the mandate`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)


-- "In such a case, it shall immediately inform ...": such a case is one where the authorised representative considers the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations (and so terminates).
-- src:446 | 4. The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation. In such a case, it shall immediately inform the relevant market surveillance authority, as well as, where applicable, the relevant notified body, about the termination of the mandate and the reasons therefor.
@ref Art 22(4) second sentence (src:446)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the authorised representative considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has informed the relevant market surveillance authority about the termination of the mandate and the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a relevant notified body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the authorised representative has informed the relevant notified body about the termination of the mandate and the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 22(4) the authorised representative has informed the relevant market surveillance authority and, where applicable, the relevant notified body of the termination and the reasons` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the authorised representative considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In such a case, it shall immediately inform the relevant market surveillance authority" (it has no reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations)
        ELSE
             IF `the authorised representative has informed the relevant market surveillance authority about the termination of the mandate and the reasons` AND ((NOT `there is a relevant notified body`) OR `the authorised representative has informed the relevant notified body about the termination of the mandate and the reasons`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it shall immediately inform the relevant market surveillance authority, as well as, where applicable, the relevant notified body, about the termination of the mandate and the reasons therefor"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)


-- The two sentences as one regulative rule: terminate, and then inform on the day of the termination ("immediately": the same day, clock of whole days; fork F-immediately).
-- The duty to terminate has no time limit stated; the duty to inform runs from the act of termination.
-- src:446 | 4. The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation. In such a case, it shall immediately inform the relevant market surveillance authority, as well as, where applicable, the relevant notified body, about the termination of the mandate and the reasons therefor.
@ref Art 22(4) (src:446)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the authorised representative considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 22 act`
`Art 22(4) the authorised representative's duty to terminate the mandate and then immediately inform` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the authorised representative considers or has reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations pursuant to this Regulation`
    THEN PARTY `Authorised representative`
         MUST `Art 22(4) terminate the mandate`
         HENCE
             PARTY `Authorised representative`
             MUST `Art 22(4) inform the relevant market surveillance authority and, where applicable, the relevant notified body about the termination and the reasons`
             WITHIN 0
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `Authorised representative` BECAUSE "the relevant market surveillance authority and, where applicable, the relevant notified body were not informed immediately about the termination of the mandate and the reasons"
         LEST BREACH BY `Authorised representative` BECAUSE "the mandate was not terminated"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the authorised representative has no reason to consider the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 22, "", 0)
